  "confidence": "verified",
  "notes": [
    "GPIO are NOT 5 V tolerant: input absolute max is IOVDD + 0.5 V; ADC pins (GP26-28) are stricter. Treat 3.6 V as the limit and level-shift any 5 V signal.",
    "GPIO drive strength is 2-12 mA (default 4 mA). Use a transistor or driver for anything larger than an indicator LED.",
    "Power: USB (VBUS), or 1.8-5.5 V into VSYS. Do not apply more than 5.5 V to VSYS. Do not back-feed VBUS while USB is connected to a computer.",
    "GP23, GP24, GP25 and GP29 are used on the board (regulator mode, VBUS sense, LED, VSYS/3 sense) and are not on the header.",
    "Pico W / Pico 2 have the same header pinout, but the Pico W LED is on the wireless chip."
  ],
